id it  they kind of ruined it for us we would  normally use them on the ground to make  the sound of the horses on whatever  surface they're on whether it's concrete  or  a dirt road or grass or something  these are three items that might not do  very much on their own but if you put  them together  get the sound  of a machine gun  being  held by a  soldier as they run along i think that's  one of the the joys of doing foley  actually is that we use these homemade  items often to create some really  beautiful sound effects  so here are a collection of different  gloves  these i would use for bird  wings  [Applause]  these are little bird call instruments  essentially they're just uh pieces of  metal that are rubbing with the on the  wood  that encloses it  little percussion instruments  most nature documentaries have full  cover foley all cameras can zoom in  really closely now the technology is  incredible obviously you've seen some of  the recent programs when they can get  into the beaks and the feathers of the  birds and things but you can't do that  with microphones in the same way so they  really have to use foley it's really  essential for nature documentaries to  make it sound real something fake to  make it sound real that's the the lovely  paradox  celery  very useful when it comes to fight  scenes makes the sounds of various  bones being broken or nose is being  punched and things we get a bit violent  with the vegetables in the studio  sometimes when it comes to zombie films  for example it's really useful to have  some celery a melon and a cabbage at  hand because you will have to  make all those gory sounds from scratch  imagine them pulling the  rib cage open and things like that also  when it comes to doing uh operations or  in something like silent witness when  they're cutting open dead bodies we also  use a lot of celery  by the way great name for the memoir  violence with the vegetables  oh thank you  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  so the stunt co